   IEEE Aerospace \& Elect Systems; South Australia Sect Joint Chapter IEEE
   Aerospace \& ElectSystems; IEEE Geoscience \& Remote Sensing Soc Japan
   Chapter; IEEE Geoscience \& Remote Sensing Soc Malaysia Chapter; IEEE
   Geoscience \& Remote Sensing Soc Gujarat Chapter; Int Cent Radio Sci},
Abstract = {The paper describes a novel two position alignment procedure on ground
   for Strapdown Inertial Navigation System. The method makes use of
   accelerometers and gyroscopes measurements from a standalone INS without
   any external aiding to obtain higher accuracy of heading angle. This
   technique mitigates the effect of down-gyroscope bias by solving
   simultaneous equations for the determination of azimuth. The accuracy is
   further improved by implementing a linear search to correct the azimuth
   dithered by the presence of gyroscope bias. The supporting simulation
   and experimental results are presented. The algorithm can be used in
   launch vehicle applications where there is a need for higher accuracy of
   azimuth prior to launch.},
