   Univ Technol, Fac Mech Engn; Univ Def Brno, Fac Military Technol},
Abstract = {The article deals with possible usage of current missile guidance
   systems and methods for unmanned aerial systems (UAS). Well known remote
   control, homing guidance or go onto location in space guidance (GOLIS)
   systems can be modified for UAS. Especially remote control and homing
   guidance systems can be used during the approach and landing phase.
   Mathematical and theoretical models of the systems were tested in the
   Webots robotic simulator using Matlab, C++ and VRML. The line of sight
   beam riding guidance (LOSBR) was chosen as a possibly appropriate system
   for autonomous UAV landing.},
