Abstract = {Aiming at the loss precision of gravity model in the Inertial Navigation
   System (INS) of the vertical hunch vehicle, a disturbing gravity,
   representation model which covers the launch area was presented in this
   paper. Even trading accuracy against speed. the results achieved by this
   method have sufficient precision for navigation calculation. By this
   means, the disturbing gravity is assigned to the navigation computation
   loop within a very short time and with an extraordinary accuracy.
   Several numerical simulations have shown that the average approximation
   error of disturbing gravity is less than 2 mGal at any height level and
