   (AIM), Kaohsiung, TAIWAN, JUL 11-14, 2012},
Organization = {I-Rice - NSC; IEEE; IES; IEEE Robot \& Automat Soc; Bur Foreign Trade;
   RDMA TW; ASME; DSC},
Abstract = {An efficient and flexible real-time guidance system is one of the
   critical needs in the development of a future reusable space
   transportation system. The genetic algorithm employs an optimization
   model called the evolution of life, which is generally considered
   numerically robust but involves an extremely high calculation cost. To
   reduce the cost, this paper proposes an efficient procedure that
   optimizes the coefficients of a set of prescribed input functions. In
   addition, to reduce the calculation time by more than one tenth, the
   optimization scheme is implemented on a field programmable gate array.
   The resultant optimization system is applied to an on-board guidance
   system that optimizes the trajectory of an experimental winged rocket in
   real time.},
