   Valley Sci \& Technol Assoc; CIS Measurement \& Instrument Comm; Beijing
   Informat Sci \& Technol Univ; Journal Elect Measurement \& Instrument},
Abstract = {Low precision of calculating angular-velocity in Gyroscope-Free
   Strap-down Inertial Navigation System (GFSINS) is always the bottleneck
   of its real application. After giving out the principle of calculating
   angular-velocity in GFSINS, a H(infinity) robust filter to improve the
   calculation precision is designed based on the analysis of a nine
   accelerometers allocation scheme. Then by use of a certain missile
   trajectory data, the simulation work in real-time is completed in four
   calculating methods (integral, extraction, standard kalman filter and
   H(infinity) robust filter) tinder the condition of white noise and
   colored noise, respectively. Analyzing all the simulation results, it is
   round that the H(infinity), robust filter has a higher calculation
   precision and better robustness.},
