Abstract = {This paper addresses auto-landing guidance, navigation and control
   design for the X34 reusable launch vehicle, including rollout dynamics.
   Vehicle requirements are summarized, along with the basic GN\&C
   architecture for the flight and rollout phases. The navigation system
   architecture is presented, along with a description of recent
   aircraft-based test results. Subsystem test results for ground steering,
   and for the NAV system, have already provided initial verification of
   portions of the landing architecture. Simulation results illustrate the
   effectiveness of the overall GN\&C design.},
