   ENGLAND, JUN 21-22, 2014},
Organization = {AASRI},
Abstract = {The H infinity filtering and Unscented Transformation(UT) algorithm are
   introduced to deal with the initial alignment error of missile-borne
   Strapdown Inertial Navigation System(SINS), which is caused by the
   nonlinear error model and the uncertainty of the disturbance noise.
   Firstly, on the basis of additional quaternion error, the error model of
   SINS is built up. Secondly, the nonlinear H infinity filter based on UT
   and H infinity filtering is constructed, which is with nonlinear
   approximation ability and strong robustness. Finally, simulations are
   made compared with UKF and the nonlinear H infinity filter under the
   conditions of disturbance model of strong wind. The result shows that
   nonlinear H infinity filter is more stable and faster than UKF under the
   disturbance conditions of strong wind and can effectively improve the
   accuracy of initial alignment and robustness of the algorithm. (C) 2014
   The Authors. Published by Elsevier B. V.},
