   SICE; HIT; UEC Tokyo; Jilin Univ; UESTC; Chinese Mech Engn Soc; State
   Key Lab Robot \& Syst; NSFC},
Abstract = {This study focuses on the coarse-precision coupling of Hemispherical
   Resonator Gyro (HRG) and Micro Electromechanical System (MEMS) Gyro for
   the new requirements of high controllability, high degree of automation,
   and diversification of combat modes for navigation systems in future
   wars, with the aim of enhancing the utility of Hemispherical Resonator
   Gyro and laying the technical foundation for the ballistic applications.
   Through the in-depth analysis of the error mechanism during the coaxial
   assembly of the two gyroscopes, this paper establishes an installation
   error model and optimizes the coupling accuracy of the two through the
   rotary scheme of the rotary table. The study improves the measurement
   accuracy by fusing the outputs of the two gyros through dual-channel
   measurement and Kalman filtering algorithm in order to estimate and
   correct the bias error of the MEMS gyro. It is experimentally verified
   that the method in this paper can effectively estimate and compensate
   the zero bias of the MEMS gyro in a low dynamic environment, thus
   improving the measurement accuracy of the MEMS gyro and the overall
   performance of the navigation system. The research results are of great
   significance to enhance the autonomous navigation capability of tactical
   missiles in complex electromagnetic environment.},
