   SOUTH AFRICA, JUL 12-17, 2009},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {Applying low-cost sensors for the navigation of aircraft is an extremely
   challenging area This paper presents an approach using dead reckoning by
   which aircraft present position may be calculated from the knowledge of
   initial position and measurements of speed and acceleration The main aim
   over here is to provide navigation information to the pilot on a cockpit
   display unit by using a standalone attitude and heading reference system
   and position estimation algorithm This is helpful in navigation when GPS
   is non-operational or GPS drops out. The navigation loop provides
   continuous and reliable navigation solutions to the guidance and flight
   control loop for the flight The whole navigation algorithm shall be
   implemented within an embedded display system that receives attitude
   information This approach is also applicable for unmanned aerial vehicle
   and self-guided-rockets, where additional air-data and engine thrust
   data can be used for additional guidance and flight control},
