Abstract = {Terrain-aided navigation is well known as an autonomous navigation
   method for aircrafts, missiles, underwater vehicles, and etc. The
   performance of iterative closest contour point (ICCP) algorithm is
   investigated in this paper deeply. The factors, including, the INS
   (inertial navigation system) precision, the map resolution, initial INS
   errors, the sonar accuracy, and the matching path length, which
   influence the matching errors, are studied for underwater vehicles.
