Abstract = {The Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory (APL) Space
   Exploration Sector traces its origins to the post-World War II
   high-altitude research using V-2 rockets. It became a major contributor
   to the U.S. space program with the development of the world's first
   satellite navigation system (Transit). During the first few decades of
   the Space Age, the Laboratory's work expanded to include significant
   contributions to the civilian space program as well as the country's
   national security. This article chronicles those accomplishments and
   discusses the core values that contributed to success.},
