Organization = {IFAC},
Abstract = {A new smooth second-order sliding mode control is proposed and proved
   using homogeneity-based technique for a system driven by sufficiently
   smooth uncertain disturbances. The main target application of this
   technique-the missile-interceptor guidance system against targets
   performing evasive maneuvers is considered. The smooth second-order
   sliding mode control-based guidance law is designed and compared with
   augmented proportional navigation guidance law via computer simulations
   of a guided missile intercepting a maneuvering ballistic target. (c)
