Abstract = {The paper analyzes the errors which have,effect on the accuracy of a
   ballistic missile with strap-down inertial navigation system during
   powered phase, and presents the transition between initial standard
   inertial launch coordinate, initial actual inertial launch coordinate
   and initial actual launch coordinate. What's more, a mathematics model
   is deduced which is used for calculating the impact, of the initial
   errors, on the precision of the missile. These formulas only rely on
   standard trajectory and are suitable for pre-launch quick correction. On
   the base, simulation models can be established. In the paper, the
   results of initial errors impact have been achieved through simulation
