Note = {12th International Conference on Advanced Materials and Engineering
   Materials-ICAMEM, THAILAND, DEC 15-18, 2023},
Abstract = {Nickel-based spinel ferrites can be applied in the Ka-band with high
   resistivity rho, high saturation magnetization 4 pi Ms, and low
   ferromagnetic resonance (FMR) linewidth Delta H and are widely applied
   in satellite communications, missile guidance systems, and on-board or
   airborne imaging radars. In this study, NiCuZn ferrites (NCZF) with the
   composition of Ni0.505Cu0.1Zn0.4Co0.015Ho0.01Fe1.97-xO4-d (x = 0.00
   similar to 0.04) were synthesized by solid-phase reaction. The
   crystalline phase formation, microstructure, magnetic and microwave
   properties of NCZF with iron deficiency are reported. The results
   demonstrated that NCZF with x = 0.01 sintered at 1050 degrees C
   possessed high 4 pi M-s (5.062 kGs), low Delta H (113 Oe), and high
   spin-wave linewidth Delta Hk (25.6 Oe).},
