   Amoiensis; APS MTT S EMC Soc Joint Nanjing Chapter},
Abstract = {A narrow-edge frequency scanning antenna is proposed in this paper. By
   introducing I-shaped resonators (ISRs), the peak gain is enhanced. A
   wide beam scan angle range is achieved by utilizing Spoof Surface
   Plasmon Polariton (SSPP) structure as the feeding line. The proposed
   antenna has a specific feature that its scanning plane is parallel to
   dielectric substrate, making it suitable in conformal occasions such as
   radar system, navigation system and missile borne system. The -10dB
   bandwidth is 12 similar to 18GHz (40\%) and the beam scanning angle is
   74 degrees in XOY plane. The simulated maximum and average gain is
   14.98dBi and 12.82dBi, respectively.},
