   Technol; Asian Control Assoc; IEEE Control Syst Soc; Inst Control Robot
   \& Syst; Soc Instrument \& Control Engineers; Chinese Assoc Automat,
   Tech Comm Control Theory; Syst Engn Soc China; Dalian Univ Technol},
Abstract = {In this paper, the multi-missiles cooperative attack problem with
   communication delay is investigated. First, the cooperative proportional
   guidance law with communication delay is proposed. And the cooperative
   guidance system is transformed into a linear time-varying system, whose
   state variables are the differences of the time-to-go of the missiles.
   Second, by using the Lyapunov theory, the asymptotic stability of the
   system is proved, that is, the time-to-go consensus of multi-missiles
   controlled by the proposed cooperative proportional guidance law is
   proved. Further, the explicit expression of the maximal tolerable delay
   is derived. Third, the effectiveness of the proposed cooperative
   proportional guidance law with communication delay is verified by
   simulation results.},
