Organization = {IEEE; Armed Forces Acad Gen Milan Rastislav Stefanik, Dept Informat;
   Slovak Electrotechnl Soc; IEEE Czechoslovakia Sect; IEEE, CAS COM SP
   Joint Chapter Czechoslovakia Sect; SophistIT; Microsoft; HP; Lynx;
   Aliter},
Abstract = {Missile guidance system, autopilot part is used for missile guidance and
   missile flight stabilization. Missile autopilot uses inertial sensors,
   gyroscopes and accelerometers for missile movement parameters
   measurements. Missile accelerometric feedback is changing according to
   accelerometer parameters, scale factor, offset and their temperature
   dependency. In this article accelerometer temperature stability,
   accelerometer white noise and their influence are explained. The article
   contribution is in creation of the missile model with accelerometric
   feedback, measurement of missile accelerometer temperature dependency,
   estimation of accelerometer white noise. According missile model
   temperature dependency (especially accelerometer temperature dependency)
   there are evaluated changes of the basic cybernetics circuit parameters,
   normal acceleration peak values, final normal acceleration values,
   missile regulation times and percentage overshoots. New accelerometer
   Simulink model is created according to accelerometer temperature
   dependency measurement and white noise estimation.},
