   Nanjing, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 12-14, 2016},
Organization = {IEEE; GNC SAA; Key Lab Sci \& Technol Natl Def; IEEE Control Syst Soc
   Chapter; Nanjing Univ Aeronaut \& Astronaut; CASC Sci \& Technol Aerosp
   Intelligent Control Lab; Beihang Univ; AVIC; ITCT, Jiangsu Key Lab;
   Chinese Soc Aeronaut \& Astronaut, Tech Comm Guidance Nav \& Control;
   Sci \& Technol Aircraft Control Lab; Chinese Assoc Automat, Tech Comm
   Control Theory; AVIC Xian Flight Automat Control Res Inst; Jiangsu Key
   Lab Internet Things \& Control Technologies},
Abstract = {The influence of the initial launching azimuth of the missile on the hit
   probability of proportional navigation under side window detection is
   studied. Side window detection will seriously reduce the hit probability
   of the guidance, thus the optimal choice of the initial launch azimuth
   of the missile is of great importance to the space interception. To get
   the optimal initial launch azimuth region, combine the angle of
   deviation of missile in both vertical and horizontal plane to form a
   great variety of initial conditions by using the line of sight as a
   benchmark. Then the applicability and distribution of the application
   range of proportional navigation under the above initial conditions are
   analyzed by simulation. Finally, the optimal initial launch azimuth
   region of missile is obtained. The research results and methods have
   some reference meaning for the optimization of the initial launching
   azimuth of the missile under side window detection.},
