Note = {28th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial-Electronics-Society,
   SEVILLE, SPAIN, NOV 05-08, 2002},
Organization = {IEEE IES; SICE; Univ Sevilla},
Abstract = {This paper is concerned with the application of robust sliding mode
   control to highly nonlinear dynamical system. Extensive research efforts
   have been made to design or improve flight guidance and control systems.
   With the phenomenal growth in soft computing techniques, there is a
   growing interest to apply these techniques to missile flight guidance
   and control systems. A fuzzy sliding mode guidance algorithm is designed
   for command-to-line-of-sight skid-to-turn (CLOS-STT) missile. The fuzzy
   logic controller is merged with a fuzzy sliding mode controller to
   improve the robustness. The acceleration command input is obtained while
   the target randomly maneuvers are considered as a source of uncertainty.
   A six-degrees-of-freedom flight model for an anti-air command guidance
   system is developed. Simulation results show the effectiveness of the
   proposed algorithm.},
