Organization = {International Federation of Automatic Control Slovakia; LISIER},
Abstract = {Three-axis Flight Motion Simulator (FMS) is a high-precision gimbal
   assembly used to replicate the 3-axis rotational movements of a
   missile/spacecraft in a laboratory environment. FMS finds use in various
   applications like calibration and testing of inertial sensors,
   HardWare-In-the-Loop testing of guidance and navigation systems, and
   implementation of Line of Sight stabilization for optoelectronic
   systems. This paper presents a mathematical model of the 3-Axis Flight
   Motion Simulator. The developed mathematical model, based on Euler's
   equations, is a coupled, non-linear model which can be used to study the
   dynamic characteristics of the FMS, model-based controller design, and
   recommend enhancements to the assembly's mechanical design for
   minimizing crosscoupling among three axes. The model has been validated
   using a detailed rigid body model. Forward and inverse dynamics
   simulation results are presented which helps in understanding the
   governing dynamics of the FMS gimbal assembly.},
