   2012},
Organization = {SPIE},
Abstract = {This paper describes the development of an USV (Unmanned Surface
   Vehicle) prototype that serves as an educational platform and can be use
   for coastal patrol and operations in the jungle. The USV length is less
   than 2 m and range of 5000 m. It's composed by the following modules:
   propulsion, power, motor driver, CPU, sensor suite, camera system,
   communication and weapon system. The weapon system is formed by an
   experimental assault rifle and a rocket launcher with a fire control
   system. The assault rifle haven't got mechanical moving parts, the
   bullets (7.62x51mm round) are electronically ignited. The CPU is an FPGA
   development kit. The USV can be operate in remote mode or fully
   autonomous. Results of some systems from laboratory and sea trials are
   show.},
