   CHINA, AUG 05-08, 2007},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Modern Tech Equipment; Chinese Assoc Higher Educ},
Abstract = {Autonomous calibration of static error mathematical model for
   accelerometer-unit in strapdown inertial navigation system (SINS) is
   discussed in this paper Considering the influence of error from
   installation of single-Axis-turntable in SINS and from installation of
   accelerometer in the single-axis-turntable, the static error
   mathematical model of accelerometer-unit is presented and its
   calibration methods are discussed. Through the error analysis, the
   requirement of installed accuracy is obtained Simulation and single
   accelerometer experiment show that these methods are effective in
   separating the static error mathematical model parameters, including
   accelerometer scale factor, bias and the second order non-linear error
   coefficient. And the approach described above can be used to carry out
   the autonomous calibration of accelerometer on missile. Therefore, it
   can improve the operation accuracy of SINS.},
