Year = {2021},
Pages = {3681-3686},
Note = {40th Chinese Control Conference (CCC), Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL
   26-28, 2021},
Organization = {TCCT; CAA; Syst Engn Soc China; Shanghai Univ; Chinese Acad Sci, Acad
   Math \& Syst Sci; China Soc Ind \& Appl Math; Asian Control Assoc; IEEE
   Control Syst Soc; Inst Control, Robot \& Syst; Soc Instrument \& Control
   Engineers; Shanghai Jiao Tong Univ; Shanghai Assoc Automat},
Abstract = {The problem of leaderless multiple missiles simultaneously attacking a
   stationary target under fixed time delay and switching directed
   communication is investigated in this paper. We firstly transform the
   missile guidance system into an equivalent system. Then based on the
   equivalent system, we design two distributed cooperative guidance laws
   in LOS direction and normal direction of LOS, respectively. The two
   cooperative guidance laws mentioned above use local neighbouring
   communications where fixed time delay and switching directed
   communication are taken into account. The former guidance law can ensure
   missiles' time-to-go converge to consensus asymptotically. The later
   guidance law can ensure missiles' relative LOS angle errors converge to
   zero asymptotically. Using the linear matrix inequalities (LMIS)
   technology, we derive the sufficient conditions of the proposed
   cooperative guidance laws. Simulation results demonstrate the
   effectiveness of the proposed cooperative guidance laws.},
