Note = {AIAA Science and Technology Forum and Exposition (AIAA SciTech Forum),
   ELECTR NETWORK, JAN 11-21, 2021},
Organization = {Amer Inst Aeronaut \& Astonaut},
Abstract = {If national governments and certain billionaires have their way, humans
   will reach Mars sometime in this century and set up permanent bases.
   Eventually they'll need a way to get around. This paper describes the
   conceptual design and analysis of a manned(10) Mars airplane configured
   for exploration, research, cargo transport, photography, and the linking
   of multiple settlements. Design development is being done by an
   international team of volunteers based on the configuration concept
   developed by lead author Dr. Daniel P. Raymer and incorporating rocket
   propulsion concepts suggested by James French. A two-man vehicle was
   developed based on overall requirements similar to the capabilities of
   the classic ``Jeep{''} of WWII fame, namely a crew of two plus cargo to
   a total of 500 lbs, carried at least 260 nmi. It is assumed that the
   flight control system will be capable of fully autonomous operation when
   desired and that when carrying humans, they need not be trained pilots.
   VTOL operation is assumed due to the deplorable lack of paved runways on
   Mars. Results to date indicate that, with sufficiently advanced
   technologies, such a manned Mars airplane should be feasible. The
   configuration presented herein seems viable ({''}existence proof{''})
   and has certain desirable features but future trade studies may find an
   even better design.},
