Abstract = {High-power amateur rocketry is an excellent route for students and young
   engineers to take their first steps in the aerospace industry. Building
   such vehicles is a complex task that requires thorough testing and
   numerous iterations. Such endeavor greatly benefits from the flexibility
   and universal nature of its components, enabling rapid integration of
   innovative solutions with the core elements of the vehicle. This paper
   presents the design of a multifunctional, modular flight computer for
   amateur bipropellant sounding rockets. With affordability, versatility,
   and stability being the key focus during the design process, this system
   can be used for a variety of projects regardless of their scale.},
