@article{ WOS:001793338700007,
Author = {Wang, Yanqing and Dong, Shi and Gao, Yuan and Du, Weifeng and Li,
   Ruixuan and Jin, He},
Title = {Method for Improving Measurement Accuracy of Star Sensors Based on Star
   Point Slice Images},
Journal = {CHINESE JOURNAL OF LASERS-ZHONGGUO JIGUANG},
Year = {2026},
Volume = {53},
Number = {6},
Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {Objective In order to achieve the target that the positioning accuracy
   of the new generation of remote sensing satellite is less than 5 m, it
   is necessary to analyze the satellite attitude control platform, global
   satellite navigation system, time reference and other measurement links.
   The measurement error of the star sensor plays a key role in the
   determination of satellite attitude. The positioning accuracy of remote
   sensing satellite is mainly determined by the on orbit measurement error
   of the star sensor. In order to improve the quality and accuracy of
   earth observation remote sensing images, and achieve high-precision
   topographic mapping and centimeter level surface deformation detection,
   it is necessary to further improve the attitude measurement accuracy of
   the star sensor. The large field of view optical system of star sensor
   will introduce a lot of nonlinear distortion, and the distortion at the
   edge of the image plane can reach more than two pixels, resulting in
   low-frequency field of view error. Due to the influence of rocket launch
   vibration, space radiation, temperature and other factors, the ground
   calibration and test parameters are no longer suitable for on orbit
   conditions. Therefore, in order to further improve the attitude accuracy
   of the satellite, it is necessary to re extract the centroid, on orbit
   calibration and attitude calculation according to the star sensor image.
   Methods The process of point slice image processing includes user
   calling program, reading the star sensitivity input information table of
   xml file, loading the original data of star map star slice image,
   obtaining centroid according to the data of wave gate image, filtering
   star centroid, correcting star distortion, calculating attitude
   quaternion, writing star sensitivity output information table of xml
   file and launching star slice image processing program. The specific
   process is shown in Figure 1. After starting the star sensor star slice
   image processing program, the user will first read the input xml
   information table file required by the star sensor, which specifies the
   name, storage path and description content through relevant protocols.
   We get the centroid from the gate image data, homogenize the gate image
   data by bilinear interpolation and other methods (see Section 2.2 for
   details), and then process the image in the gate by means of gray level
   mean and threshold segmentation. After the star sensor detects the star
   target and extracts the centroid coordinates, due to the distortion of
   the optical system, it is necessary to correct the distortion of the
   predicted navigation constant star point coordinates (see Section 2.3
   for details). After processing the multi frame data of the star slice
   image, the centroid coordinates of each detection star in the multi
   frame image are obtained, and the centroid trajectory of each detection
   star is polynomial fitted (see Section 2.4 for details), so as to
   achieve the effect of eliminating pixel high-frequency error and S-curve
   error. Results and Discussions The star sensor observes the stars on the
   ground, and calculates the total error of three axes, the noise
   equivalent angle and the low-frequency error. The total error of three
   axes is 1.50 `' for the X-axis, 1.46 `' for the Y-axis and 13.73 `' for
   the Z-axis; Three axis NEA is X-axis 1.15 `', Y-axis 1.12 `', Z-axis
   11.45 `'; The three-axis low-frequency error is 0.96 `' for the X-axis,
   0.92 `' for the Y-axis, and 7.58 `' for the Z-axis; The total error
   statistical curve is shown in Fig. 11.
   The measurement accuracy analysis after ground processing shows that the
   total error of the three axes is 0.03 `' for the X-axis, 0.02 `' for the
   Y-axis and 0.50 `' for the Z-axis; Three axis NEA is 0.01 `' for X axis,
   0.01 `' for Y-axis and 0.26 `' for Z-axis; The three-axis low-frequency
   error is 0.03 `' for the X-axis, 0.02 `' for the Y-axis and 0.42 `' for
   the Z-axis; The total error statistical curve is shown in Fig. 12. It
   can be seen from table 5 that before and after the star sensor processed
   the star point slice image ground processing algorithm, the attitude
   measurement accuracy of the outfield stargazing has been significantly
   reduced in terms of total error, noise equivalent angle, low-frequency
   error. The burrs of attitude measurement curves such as declination,
   right ascension and rolling have been significantly reduced, and the
   curve is smooth as a whole.In orbit, the equivalent angle of the
   attitude measurement noise of the star sensor is reduced from 1.18 `' to
   0.19 `', the low-frequency error of the field of view period is reduced
   from 0.99 `' to 0.48 `', and the total error of the optical axis angle
   is reduced from 1.57 `' to 0.53 `'. Table 6 shows the measurement
   accuracy statistics of the two tracks of data before and after the star
   sensor processed by the star point slice image ground processing
   algorithm. Before and after the star sensor is processed by the star
   slice image ground processing algorithm, the on orbit attitude
   measurement accuracy has been significantly reduced in terms of total
   error, noise equivalent angle and low-frequency error, and the data
   stability and consistency of the two orbits are also good. Conclusions
   Star sensor is a high-precision satellite attitude measurement sensor.
   Its measurement accuracy directly determines the accuracy of satellite
   attitude determination. Star sensor is affected by optical lens
   distortion, detector noise, image processing algorithm and other
   factors, and there is a certain measurement error. In order to meet the
   higher accuracy requirements of the new generation of remote sensing
   satellites for the star sensor, this paper proposes a processing
   algorithm based on the star point slice image. By collecting the
   original slice image of the star sensor to detect the star point area,
   the centroid coordinates of the image are re calculated, and the
   trajectory of the star point target in the field of view is fitted, the
   flicker area of the dim star target is filled, and the optical
   parameters such as focal length and distortion are corrected in real
   time. This paper expounds the image processing method of star point
   slice from the aspects of circuit, software, FPGA and algorithm. With
   the help of the powerful processing ability of ground server and image
   level raw data, the attitude measurement accuracy of star sensor is
   further improved. The use method of ground processing is introduced in
   detail, and the algorithm is compared before and after applications
   through the field observation and on orbit data. The star point slice
   image processing algorithm effectively improves the attitude measurement
   accuracy of the star sensor, which can be used by remote sensing
   satellite users to process and correct the load image on the ground,
   improve the positioning accuracy, and also provide a reference for the
   design of new space photoelectric sensor.},
