   Roberto and Di Lanzo, Domenico and Falzini, Stefano and Martini, Gialuca
   and Pagnani, Alberto and Buchanan, Neil and Sanches, Ignacio Aguillar},
Book-Group-Author = {IEEE},
Title = {Robust Telemetry System for Future Launchers},
Booktitle = {2016 7TH ESA INTERNATIONAL WORKSHOP ON TRACKING, TELEMETRY AND COMMAND
   SYSTEMS FOR SPACE APPLICATIONS (TTC)},
Year = {2016},
Note = {7th ESA International Workshop on Tracking, Telemetry and Command
   Systems for Space Applications (TTC), Noordwijk, NETHERLANDS, SEP 13-16,
   2016},
Organization = {IEEE; European Space Agcy; ESTEC},
Abstract = {This article presents a consideration of a new robust telemetry (TM)
   system for future launchers. The main target is to increase the maximum
   data rate of TM system to at least 5 Mbps with improvements such as more
   efficient physical layer, advanced antenna solutions, lossless data
   compression, satellite relays, and adaptive coding and modulation (ACM).
   An extension module for Network Simulator 3 (ns-3) for launch vehicle
   (LV) TM communications was developed, which is capable of evaluating the
   system performance and potential gains of the proposed enhancements. The
   results show that the proposed telemetry system can reach close to the
   target capacity with new physical layer modulation and coding scheme and
   the performance may be further improved with retrodirective antenna
   array and satellite relays.},
