   OCT 01-05, 2001},
Organization = {Int Acad Astronaut Comm Safety \& Qual},
Abstract = {In this presentation, we define radiation environments encountered by
   the European heavy lift carrier ARIANE 5, which are illustrative of
   future missions to be handled by this type of launcher.
   The presentation will show the different types of radiation environments
   affecting ARIANE 5 depending of the launcher's mission.
   Furthermore, this presentation describes the approach used for ARIANE 5
   launch vehicle to overcome the risks from natural radiation environment,
   that is to say essentially, cosmic rays, Van Allen protons belt, and
   solar activity.
   The second part of this presentation is relative to atmospheric
   environment; It has been demonstrated that the failures (Single Event
   Upset) occurring on the electronics are caused by neutrons. Upsets
   registered by computer memories are causing more and more concern in the
   avionics industry. In this field, as elsewhere, electronic devices are
   playing an ever more significant role, involving increasingly
   sophisticated components.
   The presentation will describe what is usually called atmospheric
   shower, the way it is taken into account at a specification point of
   view, and some results obtained on very recent experiments realized in
   Europe. Future projects, which aim is to measure atmospheric radiation
   environment species will be also presented.},
