Organization = {European Space Agcy},
Abstract = {In autumn 2003 Lockheed Martin Michoud Operations (LM), Andoya Rocket
   Range (ARR) and Nammo Raufoss (NARA) initiated the Norwegian Sounding
   Rocket (NSR) program for transferring hybrid rocket technology from LM
   in US to NARA in Norway. LM was responsible for the training and design,
   while NARA was responsible for building the rocket using domestic
   suppliers. ARR was responsible for building the telemetry payload as
   well as for performing the launch operation.
   On 30.August 2005 NSR was successfully static tested at NARA Test
   Center, followed by a program hold due to lack of funding. However, in
   late 2006 new funding was in place and the Hybrid Test Rocket (HTR)
   program was initiated with the intention to launch the rocket from
   Andoya Norway within May 2007. A successful launch occurred on schedule
   03.May 2007.},
