   POLAND, MAY 14-17, 2018},
Abstract = {Antennas for Global Navigation Satellite Systems are critical for
   sounding rockets and missiles. Due to limited space available within the
   structure, microstrip antennas offer several benefits in providing an
   inexpensive method for telemetry and satellite positioning systems. Most
   of the wraparound microstrip antennas are linearly polarized due to
   rotation of the structure. However, advanced receivers can resolve
   missile rotation if the antenna supports circular polarization of GNSS.
