Organization = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc},
Abstract = {This paper discusses the design and development of Avionic Systems that
   are amenable for reconfiguration. The avionic system for any space
   mission is composed of inter-connected subsystems that perform a
   specific function that is a part of the intended functionality. For
   instance, the telemetry system is composed of sensors, signal
   conditioners, digitizers, data aggregators and RF transmitter systems
   that constitute the end-to-end signal chain. We examine how
   state-of-the-art technologies like mixed-domain VLSI and Embedded
   systems with advanced interfaces can be utilized for realization of all
   these subsystems with soft programmable features so as to render the
   entire system reconfigurable from end-to-end. Such a system design gives
   enormous advantages ranging from reuse of hardware from mission to
   mission to on-the-fly reconfiguration to satisfy the requirements during
   various phases of a specific mission. This is especially important in
   the context of advanced space missions like Re-entry Launch Vehicles
   (RLV), Space Stations and Lunar and Inter-planetary missions.},
