Organization = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc; IEEE Aerospace
   and Electronic Systems Society; IEEE Poland Section},
Abstract = {The tracking of sounding rockets during the launch phase remains an
   important aspect of communications, the collection of telemetry data
   during the launch, and the safety of the flight. In order to
   automatically track aerial vehicles, a Direction of Arrival (DoA)
   solution is commonly used. In this paper, we propose the design and
   implementation of a fully functional DoA system which determines the
   elevation and azimuth angles of the signal source at the operational
   frequency f(0) = 2.4 GHz for the tracking of rocket sounds and other
   applications. For the system to operate properly, the entire radio path
   was design, starting from the antenna, through the amplifying,
   measuring, acquisition elements, and ending with the software. The
   proposed measurement system utilizes a five-port microstrip correlator
   as its core component, representing an uncommon design choice. The
   objective of this study is to evaluate its performance and
   effectiveness.},
