   26-30, 2016},
Organization = {Int Acad Astronaut},
Abstract = {This chapter will portray the activities of rocketry as an educational
   and research tool at the Technion Israel's Institute of Technology, from
   the 1980s through the 1990s the late period of this type of activity at
   the Technion. From a modest beginning in the late 1960s, the faculty in
   the aeronautics department used to build student research rockets as a
   hands-on project. The rockets became bigger and more sophisticated, and
   many new features were included, such as: telemetry, avionics, and
   multi-staging. The rockets of the Technion were designed by faculty,
   staff, and students. Some assistance in the field of casting solid
   propellants was provided by the Israeli defense industries, and the
   military offered use of its test ranges. This chapter is the third in a
   series of articles by the author, tracking the research rockets projects
   conducted in Israel from the 1960s to the late 1990s, and beyond.},
