   2015},
Organization = {Neelain Univ; IEEE Sudan Subsect},
Abstract = {The attitude determination and control system is required by a satellite
   in order to monitor and control its orientation during orbiting around
   Earth. It operates in a similar manner of the autopilot used by aircraft
   and missiles. Sensors determine attitude of satellite, while actuators
   act to modify the orientation of it to point at a reference direction.
   For small satellites such as nanosatellites, and cube satellites in
   particular, the size and weight of sensors and actuators are so limited.
   Thus, the selection of the right sensors and actuators as well as the
   processor is a very crucial task in the design of the attitude
   determination and control subsystem of a cube satellite. Hardware
   selection is vital due to existence of various sensors, actuators and
   processors that are applied in satellites.},
