Number = {5},
Pages = {5279-5291},
Month = {SEP 1},
Abstract = {The paper describes two methods for determining the rotational axis of
   an object in flat spin, for a H-2A R/B and cylindrical bodies in
   general. Both methods can be applied and extended to the case of free
   precession, a procedure which is presented in this work. One method is
   based on the change of the brightness of the object during one rotation
   period, the second is based on the time between two specular flashes of
   the object. In order to apply the methods, input data in the form of
   photometric measurements are required. For this study, we used data from
   the Mini-MegaTORTORA (MMT) catalogue as well as observations obtained
   with the AGO70 telescope, which are subsequently processed and published
   in the Space Debris Light Curve Database (SDLCD). (c) 2026 COSPAR.
