Abstract = {ADEOS (Advanced Earth Observing Satellite) was launched on 17 August
   1996 by an H-II rocket from the Tanegashima Space Center. After the
   satellite operated for 10 months, the operation stopped on 30 June 1997.
   After investigation with telemetry data, it was found that the loss of
   power caused by the fracture of a solar array paddle was attributed to
   the anomaly. In this paper, we describe the results of the analysis with
   the telemetry data of satellite attitude to find the cause of anomaly of
