Organization = {Japanese Rocket Soc; Chinese Soc Astronaut; Amer Astronaut Soc},
Abstract = {The ALOS, Advanced Land Observing Satellite, is a Japanese solution to
   high-resolution earth observation. It is equipped with three mission
   instruments: Panchromatic Remote sensing Instrument for Stereo Mapping
   (PRISM), Advanced Visible and Near Infrared Radiometer type 2 (AVNIR-2)
   and Phased Array type L-band Synthetic Aperture Radar (PALSAR) for
   achieving its mission includes cartography, regional observation and
   disaster monitoring. In order to fully utilize the data obtained by
   these sensors, the ALOS are given mass data handling capability and
   high-precision position and attitude determination subsystem which are
   necessary to high resolution remote sensing satellites in the next
   decade. The ALOS will be launched by the Japanese H-LIA rocket in 2003.},
