   the current successor to Cute-1.7 + APD. This new satellite is based on
   its predecessor but has some modifications to increase its reliability
   and robustness against radiation effects, electrical power shortage and
   so on. The satellite was launched by an ISRO PSLV-C9 rocket on April 28,
   2008 and has operated for more than 9 months. Throughout its operation,
   many missions such as attitude determination and control experiments,
   scientific observations, photographing and communication experiments
