Abstract = {Sharing of know-how 700 persons among which two thirds of DGA (incl. 45
   Engineers) and one third of Navy personnel (incl. 14 officers).
   Outstanding settlement In Toulon the technical building of the
   Mourillon:
   Heading, administrative services, data post-processing,
   movie-photography laboratory.
   On the LEVANT ISLAND, the main base which accomodates the main computer,
   the test means and the firing positions on 940 hectares (2322 acres).
   On the top of the MOUNT COUDON (700 meters high):a radio-telemetry
   station and space surveillance facilities.
   On PORT-CROS and PORQUEROLLES ISLANDS: two optical stations.
   On the Peninsula of SAINT-MANDRIER :small calibre firing range of La
   Renardiere.
   In CORSICA, at COTI-CHIAVARI: station manned on request for long range
   firings.
   CEM enjoys an outstanding geographical settlement due to: the vicinity
   of deep waters (2 400 m) and high points (700 m); the location inside an
   air area (D54) controlled by the Navy; military surroundings: naval air
   forces, DCN development centers, air test center of Istres, 54th
   Artillery Battalion and Hyeres Naval Air Station;
   good weather conditions.
   CEM Activities
   The CEM operations are distributed between:
   new weapon systems development tests;
   training firings for operational weapons;
   electronic warfare training and FORACS.
   The weapons systems involve tactical missiles and torpedoes launched
   from: Surface ship: MM15, MM38, MM40, OTOMAT, SADRAL, CROTALE, STANDARD
   MISSILE, SEA SPARROW, MASURCA, MILAS, GUNS, TORPEDOES
   Submarines: SM39, TORPEDOES, DECOYS, DETECTION EQUIPMENT, SONAR.
   Aircrafts: AS12, AS15, AS37, AM39, PENGUIN, SPARROW, MAGIC, M530, SUPER
   530, ASMP, MU90, TORPEDOES, SONAR.
   Ground from Levant Island: ROLAND, CROTALE, MISTRAL, MLRS 155 mm SHELLS.
   Assembly of facilities Threat simulation : Airbone: high performances
   targets: C22, light targets: FOX.
   Surface: towed catamaran, decommissioned warships, remote controlled
   self-defense test ship.
   Underwater: CII and CALAS targets.
   Electronics: Electronic Warfare Generator SIRENE. Tracking: 7 radars, 10
   kinetheodolites, 8 infrared trackers Minilir, differential GPS, 3
   underwater ranges TREMAIL. Observation: 4 telescopes, 115 fixed cameras,
   31 video cameras. Telemetry: 7 antennas. Flight termination systems: 2
   stations.
   Data acquisition and processing centers: A double control room, 2
   telemetry observation rooms, 1 data processing center, 1
   photography-movie laboratory.
   Meteorology: Aerological measurements, meteorological observations and
   forecast. Facilities: Surveillance of areas: radars, ships, helicopters,
   aircraft. Ground and sea transportation provided by CEM.
   Hosting and restauration on Levant Island. Excellence fields Air and
   underwater tracking. Optical measurements. Events measurements.
   Telemetry reception. Real size simulation of the battle field.
   Large areas allowing air, surface and underwater firings and trainings
   with unique equipment in Europe.
   Highly professional service working towards ISO 9001 certification.
   Engineering Design of suitable test disposals. Proficiency in test
