   (IMEKO), Inst Measurement \& Control, Belfast, ENGLAND, SEP 03-06, 2018},
Abstract = {Measurement of mechanical quantities such as speed, acceleration,
   angular velocity and also orientations is of crucial importance in many
   applications and in particular in robotics. In order to illustrate
   different direct and indirect approaches (integration and
   differentiation methods) we use an air rocket experiment for a bachelor
   level university laboratory course. Besides getting familiar with image
   based measurement, remote measurement and telemetry, the experiment also
   provides hands-on experience with Newton's axioms. A further aspect is
   the evaluation and comparison of the obtained data, also with respect to
   uncertainty, drift, etc. Using a fun experiment, it is aimed to get more
   students interested in the topic.},
