Organization = {YASHADA, MDC, IEEE Pune Sect; IEEE},
Abstract = {In this paper design and development of an S Band linearly polarized
   microstrip patch antenna for high temperature applications is presented
   with simulated and measured results. The antenna requires dielectric
   cover over radiating portion to provide the protection from heat,
   physical damage and environment. This antenna configuration is mostly
   useful in applications like missiles, aircrafts, spacecrafts and
   satellites. The proposed antenna configuration is designed and optimized
   by simulation studies using IE3D which is based on the Finite Element
   Method (FEM). The radiation performance of single antenna, 4 element
