   PART A},
Year = {1994},
Volume = {17},
Number = {3},
Pages = {398-403},
Month = {SEP},
Note = {Nonvolatile Memory Technology Review, BALTIMORE, MD, JUN 22-24, 1993},
Abstract = {A practical alternative to telemetry is being used during the flight
   testing of a new autonomous antitank munition for the capture of onboard
   test data. A unique crash-proof solid state flight data recorder (FDR)
   using nonvolatile flash EPROM memory was developed and extensively
   tested and has been successfully used on five full system flight tests
   to date. The FDR stores over 20 megabytes of flight data in the tactical
   missile's warhead volume and retains all data even after a high-speed
   impact with steel armor plating. Serial digital data from the missile's
   onboard processor and various onboard sensors is captured at a rate
   greater than 6 mb/s.},
