Abstract = {NAROM (Norwegian Centre for Space Related Education) was formed in 2000
   to organize space related educational activities, to promote
   recruitment, to promote appreciation for the benefits of space
   activities, and to stimulate interest for science in general. NAROM and
   Andoya Rocket Range (ARR) have since 1997 developed and launched more
   than 20 student rockets. Hundreds of students have had theoretical
   introductory and hands-on work preparing for the launch of a student
   rocket at ARR. Two modifications of the student rocket are made the
   summer 2005, including change of rocket engine and change to S-band
   telemetry. The main goal of the Student Rocket Program is to give the
   students a comprehensive introduction to an ordinary scientific rocket
   launch from ARR.},
