Volume = {31},
Number = {1},
Pages = {23-44},
Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {We present a suborbital rocket payload capable of performing soft X-ray
   spectroscopy on extended sources. The payload can reach resolutions of
   similar to 100 (lambda/ Delta lambda) over sources as large as 3.25A
   degrees in diameter in the 17-107 bandpass. This permits analysis of the
   overall energy balance of nearby supernova remnants and the detailed
   nature of the diffuse soft X-ray background. The main components of the
   instrument are: wire grid collimators, off-plane grating arrays and
   gaseous electron multiplier detectors. This payload is adaptable to
   longer duration orbital rockets given its comparatively simple pointing
   and telemetry requirements and an abundance of potential science
   targets.},
