   and Zhang, Bin},
Title = {A Hybrid-Domain Algorithm for High-Speed High-Squint SAR Imaging With
   Curved Trajectory via Fifth-Order FNCS Processing},
Journal = {IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON GEOSCIENCE AND REMOTE SENSING},
Year = {2026},
Volume = {64},
Abstract = {Because of the severe 2-D range-azimuth coupling (RAC) and Doppler
   space-variance (DSV), high-speed high-squint (HSHS) synthetic aperture
   radar (SAR) imaging with curved trajectory is still extremely
   problematic. To address this issue, a hybrid-domain algorithm via
   fifth-order frequency nonlinear chirp scaling (FNCS) processing is
   proposed in this article. The proposed algorithm comprises three
   modules: range focusing, azimuth compression, and geometric correction
   (GC). To enhance model accuracy while simplifying the coefficient
   representation, a fifth-order slant range model based on equivalent
   velocity and parameter vectorization is initially established. After the
   preprocessing employed to remove bulk RAC, range focusing is
   accomplished using a range-variant Stolt interpolation. Then, to
   eliminate DSV for azimuth compression, a fifth-order FNCS processing is
   presented based on a minimalist derivation approach. This approach
   derives an explicit expression for the FNCS-processed signal directly
   from the determined model and NCS orders to aid in the solution of
   undetermined parameters. Subsequently, an instantaneous projection
   geometry is proposed for GC, with the capability to eliminate arbitrary
   geometric distortions. Finally, the results of processing simulation and
   real SAR data demonstrate the validity and superiority of the proposed
   algorithm.},
